From 407ce3ff32abfce8f967d12472a6ec7ac629c7a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:03:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] IOWIDGET-3: the IO buttons that need the safe door are
 coloured like golden; TestSuck with an IC on the Index runs golden's Suck() /
 Destroy()
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20261001 picked both: 「填安全門表＋橘黃色」, 「TestSuck 走 Suck() 流程」.

- JsonBridge/ChanIoPoints.cpp: /api/struct/io/config gives every output hw.needSafeDoor =
  golden's bIdleNeedCheckSafeDoor (filled by InitCylinder, which wb_serve runs through
  InitialHandler). Read by golden's own arithmetic: the ISA family [0][Port/32][Port%32][Bit],
  MotionNet / 1203 [Ring][IP][Port][Bit] NOT range-checked -- golden's writer (cinitial.cpp:5451)
  and the reader that blocks the output (IdleCheckSafeDoorByCylinder via MyLaneIo.cpp:261/:326)
  both index it raw, so a 1203 row past [64][32] (HT9050: IP 176) is read at the same cell of the
  64 KB block; past the block = not marked. The page (web ht9045_io_widgets.js) paints such a
  button golden's orange / yellow with black text (iosetview.cpp:2244-2258).
- JsonBridge/IoBtnPanelClick.cpp: TestSuck *_On / *_Off while the Index holds an IC = golden
  iosetview.cpp:1040-1083: the sucker of that name (FTestSuck rows x cols; F_On, B_On, F_Off,
  B_Off) gets its Suck() / Destroy() sequence instead of a raw coil write; no such sucker = refused
  (golden does nothing). W906_IoTestSuckTick() = golden Timer1Timer :159-173, run every pass.
  Not a guard, so W906_IO_PAGE_NO_GUARDS does not skip it. DEVIATION (b) retired.
- tools/wb_serve.cpp: W906_IoTestSuckTick() at the two PumpTick lines (same line, no line moves).

Offline test (scratch, the versioned machines/HT9050/IO_Table.csv, no card, no wb_serve, writes
nothing; production_audit before / after: every machine file's MD5 unchanged): 17/17.
  needSafeDoor follows the table, an input never; a golden-style mark on a 1203 row at IP 176 is
  read; InitCylinder on the HT9050 table marks no cell at all (the 7 enabled cylinders all sit on
  golden's bypass list, none past the table) -> on this machine no button is door-gated today.
  TestSuck: FTestSuckAA_On -> Suck() done after 7 ticks (DUMMY run), FTestSuckAB_Off -> Destroy(),
  an unknown TestSuck alias refused, no IC -> the ordinary path.
A scratch wb_serve links (W906_IoTestSuckTick, NeedSafeDoor in the image). The running machine
build was not touched: it needs F5 (rebuild + restart) to take this.
Note: the HT9050 TestSuck *_On / *_Off rows are Enable=0, and Sensor() answers true for a
disabled sucker, so Destroy() ends at once there -- faithful.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
